# MIDI LED Teensy — agent guide

## Entry points

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/latest.ino` | **All firmware logic** (~1,190 lines, single file by design) |
| `src/name.c` | USB device name only — Teensy requires a separate `.c` tab |
| `docs/architecture.html` | Architecture report — read before large changes |
| `README.md` | MIDI mapping, SD layout, contributor workflow |
| `tools/` | Python media prep — **not** flashed to device |

## Hardware (current)

- Teensy 4.1 + OctoWS2811 + WS2811 matrix
- Logical display: **40×96** (3,840 LEDs), 8 panels in serpentine wiring
- DAW → USB MIDI; optional SD card + 2 Mbaud serial video stream

## `latest.ino` structure

Keep new code in the matching section (do not scatter):

1. Configuration constants
2. Types + global state
3. Forward declarations
4. Coordinate / color utilities (`mapXYtoLedIndex`, `sampleLayer`, `applyHSVAdjustments`, …)
5. Media utilities (`buildMediaPath`, `findMapping`, …)
6. MIDI handlers (`handle*NoteEvent`, `handleControlChange`, `dispatchNoteEvent`)
7. Media I/O (`startVideo`, `handleSDVideo`, `handleSerialVideo`, …)
8. Compositing (`updateLEDs`)
9. `setup()` / `loop()`

## Coding conventions

- **C++17 max** — Teensyduino does not support C++20; no concepts, `std::span`, designated initializers (C++20 style), `consteval`, etc.
- **Stay in one file** unless the user explicitly asks to split
- **DRY**: reuse existing helpers; add small helpers in the utilities section
- **Minimal diffs** — no drive-by refactors or unrelated cleanup
- Match existing naming: `camelCase` functions, `UPPER_SNAKE` MIDI constants
- New MIDI CC/channel → update README MIDI tables + this rule if needed
- Frame size: `FRAME_BYTES = width * height * 3` (11,520 bytes)
- Map filenames: **8.3 only** (`char filename[13]`) — e.g. `cube.bin`, not `my-long-video.bin`

## Layer compositing (do not break silently)

Bottom → top in `updateLEDs()`: video → image (alpha) → LED blocks → strobe overlay.

- `handleSerialVideo()` **bypasses** the layer stack (fast path) — intentional
- Strobe uses `strobeActive[]` + `strobeBaseStates[]`, not `groupStates`
- LED blocks use **per-channel** HSV (not combined RGB HSV)

## Safe change patterns

```cpp
// New strobe region → add row to STROBE_PATTERNS[]
// New media type → reuse sampleLayer() + updateLEDs layer slot
// New note mapping → extend handler + video_map.txt / image_map.txt format
// New CC → handleControlChange() + README CC table
```

## Do not without explicit user request

- Split firmware into multiple tabs/files (except `name.c`)
- Unify serial video through `updateLEDs()` (changes live-stream behavior)
- Remove legacy equal-RGB block strobe branch in `updateLEDs()`
- Create git commits or push
- Edit `docs/architecture.html` unless updating architecture docs

## After firmware changes

Suggest hardware smoke test: startup blue flash, MIDI ch 1–6, SD video loop, image layer, serial stream timeout.
